From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 02:11:52 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 12/46] mobile: pinch zoom stays under the fingers

onTwoFingerScaleUpdate anchored the zoom on the global focal point, but the
canvas lives inside SafeArea, so the content slid away from the fingers by the
inset (up to 59 pt on Dynamic Island iPhones, also in landscape). The local
focal point is the canvas' own coordinate.

(Research patch ios-touch 0003.)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 flutter/lib/common/widgets/remote_input.dart | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/flutter/lib/common/widgets/remote_input.dart b/flutter/lib/common/widgets/remote_input.dart
index f311d39..a3d9e4c 100644
--- a/flutter/lib/common/widgets/remote_input.dart
+++ b/flutter/lib/common/widgets/remote_input.dart
@@ -493,7 +493,7 @@ class _RawTouchGestureDetectorRegionState
       }
     } else {
       // mobile
-      ffi.canvasModel.updateScale(d.scale / _scale, d.focalPoint);
+      ffi.canvasModel.updateScale(d.scale / _scale, d.localFocalPoint);
       _scale = d.scale;
       ffi.canvasModel.panX(d.focalPointDelta.dx);
       ffi.canvasModel.panY(d.focalPointDelta.dy);
